{"issue": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764", "id": 3907822741, "node_id": "I_kwDOBabE0s7o7KSV", "number": 2764, "title": "Log file download resume after a partial download?", "user": {"login": "flybratten04", "id": 71947627, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTQ3NjI3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71947627?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04", "html_url": "https://github.com/flybratten04", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 629977272, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw2Mjk5NzcyNzI=", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/labels/question", "name": "question", "color": "cc317c", "default": true, "description": null}], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 4, "created_at": "2026-02-06T17:51:18Z", "updated_at": "2026-04-02T08:10:19Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-02T08:10:19Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Julian/Gents:\n I don't know if the community is interested in such a capability as it is sort of a unique situation. Our drones have an associated Raspberry Pi, so when powered but not armed, we download the log files from Ardupilot to the Pi over a serial port (implied relatively slow). Our log files can grow to 200MB or so, hence it is quite possible for an operator to power down while a download is in progress, hence leaving a partial file.\n I modified (hopefully not a hack) the logfile plugin to support a resume of downloading from where the partial download ended. From the initial tests the code appears robust, but this is only against a simulator and not field tests.\n If there is interest I would certainly share the approach and the code with the community where it could reviewed potentially improved. \n\nCheers, ", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null}, "comments": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3865607328", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764#issuecomment-3865607328", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764", "id": 3865607328, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s7maHyg", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-02-07T22:06:47Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-07T22:06:47Z", "body": "I'd be ok merging this if it doesn't introduce too much complexity or other problems.\n\nThat being said, I think we should probably move to the MAVLink FTP protocol instead of using the clunky log files messages, because that one features CRC checks and partial downloads out of the box. We could even implement MAVSDK to support resuming downloading a file with FTP.", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3865607328/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3874910375", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764#issuecomment-3874910375", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764", "id": 3874910375, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s7m9nCn", "user": {"login": "flybratten04", "id": 71947627, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTQ3NjI3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71947627?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04", "html_url": "https://github.com/flybratten04", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/flybratten04/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-02-10T02:09:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-10T02:09:05Z", "body": "Actually, I would much prefer FTP as well, but for the Ardupilot it is painfully slow (I assume it is the Ardupilot server code and not the MAVSDK). I ran the simple Linux time command on ~40MB log file:\n\n- logfile_download: ~45 seconds\n- ftp_client: 33 minutes\nIs ftp for PX4 extremely slow as well or is the performance comparable to the MavLink Log_Data packet implementation?\nCurrently there are only minimal changes to log_files_impl.cpp. All most all of the work is done in the examples/logfile_download.cpp file. Maybe this is a good thing, though I'm not all the happy with the code. \n If the ftp performance with PX4 is good enough then maybe the Ardupilot ftp server will be improved someday as well. That would make this work irrelevant assuming ftp supports resuming.\n", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3874910375/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3875017371", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764#issuecomment-3875017371", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2764", "id": 3875017371, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s7m-BKb", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url